#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# mangoldt_lambda

#% text
# `mangoldt_lambda(n)` gives the von Mangoldt function: `log(p)` when `n` is a power of the prime `p`, otherwise 0.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is exact: `log(2)` for `n = 8`.

#% item
# `mangoldt_lambda` is listable.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
mangoldt_lambda(8)
#% output
#= log(2)

#% cell
mangoldt_lambda(12)
#% output
#= 0

#% cell
mangoldt_lambda(7)
#% output
#= log(7)

#% cell
mangoldt_lambda(range(10))
#% output
#= [0, log(2), log(3), log(2), log(5), 0, log(7), log(2), log(3), 0]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# Its sum over the divisors of `n` is `log(n)`:

#% cell
simplify(divisor_sum(360, mangoldt_lambda) - log(360))
#% output
#= 0

#% text
# Chebyshev's function, the partial sum, is close to `x`:

#% cell
n(sum(mangoldt_lambda(range(10000))))
#% output
#= 10013.396693263108

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `is_prime_power`, `moebius_mu`, `prime_pi`
